Fonts vendored into Enclave
===========================

Every font file in this directory is licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1. The full licence text is reproduced at the bottom of this file; it
is identical for all three families, so it is included once.

Fonts
-----

Inter                  -- Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors
                          https://github.com/rsms/inter
                          Principal author: Rasmus Andersson
                          SIL Open Font License 1.1

Inter Tight            -- Copyright 2022 The Inter Project Authors
                          https://github.com/rsms/inter-tight
                          Principal author: Rasmus Andersson
                          SIL Open Font License 1.1

JetBrains Mono         -- Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors
                          https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
                          Authors: Philipp Nurullin, Konstantin Bulenkov
                          (JetBrains s.r.o.)
                          SIL Open Font License 1.1

None of the three declares a Reserved Font Name, so the OFL's renaming clause
does not bite. The files here are verbatim upstream binaries -- nothing was
re-encoded, re-hinted or otherwise modified -- so we are a redistributor under
OFL section 2, and this notice plus the licence text is what that requires.

Why these files are in the repository at all
--------------------------------------------

Enclave must not fetch anything from a third-party CDN at page load. Doing so
leaks every user's IP address to that CDN, breaks air-gapped installs outright,
and contradicts the data-residency commitment in docs/08-BYO-INFRA.md section 18.
Serving the fonts from our own origin is the only arrangement that holds in all
three cases. See ENC-135.

Provenance
----------

Fetched from the Google Fonts CSS2 API on 2026-08-19, which serves each family
as a variable font already split by Unicode range:

  https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2
      ?family=Inter:wght@400..600
      &family=Inter+Tight:wght@500..600
      &family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400..500
      &display=swap

requested with a Chrome user agent so the API returned woff2. Binaries were then
downloaded from fonts.gstatic.com:

  Inter          v20
  Inter Tight    v9
  JetBrains Mono v24

Each file is a variable font carrying the whole weight range the design system
uses, so one file replaces what would otherwise be three static weights. Files
are named <family>-<unicode-range>.woff2 and the @font-face rules that reference
them carry the matching unicode-range, so a browser downloads only the ranges a
page actually renders -- an English page pulls the three latin files (about
122 KB) and nothing else.

The non-Latin ranges are vendored even though the design reference is written in
English, because they cost nothing until they are needed and their absence would
be an i18n regression against docs/14-I18N-L10N.md the first time a locale lands.

No further subsetting was applied. Cutting these down by glyph coverage needs
pyftsubset or an equivalent, which means a build step; that is deliberately out
of scope here and belongs with the SPA build.

